Z||000000||FIERO1985||02-26-2001||04:48 PM||||Recently on my 85 gt 4 speed I noticed that when I shift over to reverse it gets harder to shift and it sticks in place and you literally have to shove it back over to slect the 4 driving gears. The car shifts through that 4 fine but if I move it laterally back and forth it becomes stuck I disassembled and found that it is not in the console imediate area but back towards the Slave? bracket where the two cables run. I know that there is a piston that goes up and down but what should I do to correct this problem!!<P>Thanks for any help!!<P>Dan<BR>85 gt 4speed<P>------------------<BR>1985 GT V6 <BR>"LETS RACE"||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||02-26-2001||04:55 PM||||it could be several things, possilby a worn out sincro (bad), or just a cable problem.<P>get someone to sit in the car and change gears, while you watch the cables.  this will help in determining if it is an external problem.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||FIERO1985||02-26-2001||04:57 PM||||arent there bushings involved also!?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||02-26-2001||06:00 PM||||First off follow the procedure in the manual and re-adjust the cables.  If this doesn't help then look at the levers where the cables attach at the transmission end.  Do you see any worn out bushings?  Does everything move smoothly?  There are no pistons involved in shifting.||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-26-2001||06:52 PM||||while it's apart clean and lube whatever parts get it. ||||reg||1
